  "description": "FFmpeg shared libraries and the bundled ffmpeg/ffprobe tools for FrameFlow develop-time use. sha256 is of the extracted file, not the archive, and changes with every build - regenerate the affected RIDs when a pin moves. The tools are listed alongside the libraries because fetch-ffmpeg.cs installs them too and generate-test-corpus.cs executes ffmpeg. Two pins, not one: win/linux come from the BtbN build named by buildTag/archiveVersion, and osx-arm64 from this repo's own LGPL build (scripts/build-ffmpeg-macos.sh) published as a GitHub Release - it carries libraries only, links no external libraries, and is LGPL-2.1 rather than the BtbN build's LGPL-3-and-Apache-2.0. osx-x64 does not exist: Intel macOS was dropped in 2026-09 and fetch-ffmpeg.cs rejects the RID. The BtbN hashes are for the LGPL build only; a --license gpl run is unverified by design.",
